File: contrib/libtests/pngstest.c
Line: 3225
Function: write_one_file
Bug type: stack-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-121
Explanation: A fixed-size stack buffer 'name[32]' is written using sprintf without bounds: sprintf(name, "%s%u.png", tmpf, ++counter). If the prefix 'tmpf' plus the decimal digits of 'counter' and the suffix '.png' exceed 31 characters, this overflows 'name', corrupting stack memory.

